Z||000000||TRL46202||09-18-2000||10:11 AM||||(87GT 5spd)Tranny was pulled all the normal stuff was replaced, etc... runs and drives fine/great and shifts fine but I do notice that I have to push the clutch almost all the way to the floor for it to shift. Is this normal or what? I know the clutch has been addressed in other posts but I haven't seen one, (maybe I'm blind) that just talks about pedal play.....<P>Thanks! Tom||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||09-19-2000||12:12 AM||||I think that's fairly normal behavior for a brand new clutch.  Let the pedal come up an inch(?) off the floor, and it begins to engage.||||reg||14
