Z||000004||Tina||12-27-2000||09:34 PM||||Usually adjustable.<BR>Just bring it back to the shop<P>A little less play, please!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||2birds||12-27-2000||09:47 PM||||I had to bleed air out of mine each time I replaced the clutch.  A Mity-Vac works great for this.  Don't exactly know why, since the hydraulics weren't touched at all, but maybe because the slave cylinder got turned all around and hung there for a while. Had to replace the slave the last time, due to a rusty bleeder screw.  Works great now.  The flywheel has been resurfaced three times, no shims used, and it is nonadjustable, other than shimming the flywheel or stuffing something in between the slave pushrod and the throwout bearing actuator.  Clutch starts to grab about 1/2 pedal travel.<p>[This message has been edited by 2birds (edited 12-27-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||2xsess||12-28-2000||01:36 AM||||Try bleeding it.<P>Gravity Bleeding is so easy. That's the way I did mine after I replaced the slave.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by 2xsess (edited 12-28-2000).]||||reg||1
